ub.com/users/afterow","html_url":"https://github.com/afterow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T10:53:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T10:53:19Z","body":"**Suggestion for Documentation Workflow**  \r\nI apologize for submitting the PR without prior discussion. I wanted to suggest a workflow where:  \r\n1. The team updates only the `en/` directory for English documentation.  \r\n2. The `zh/` directory (for Chinese) is configured as a **Git submodule** pointing to my translation repository.  \r\n\r\nThis way:  \r\n- Your team can freely update English docs without conflicts.  \r\n- Once the `en/` docs are updated, I can submit corresponding Chinese translations via the submodule.  \r\n- It maintains synchronization while avoiding merge issues.  \r\n\r\nWould this approach work for the project?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2710172370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"afterow","id":99971730,"node_id":"U_kgDOBfVykg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99971730?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/afterow","html_url":"https://github.c